{"event": "report", "t": 1795260242.559, "claim": "fixed", "text": "_unit_price`.\n- Units sold (5,460) and revenue ($643,615.84) match an independent query over the same filtered order lines.\n- Variant total (1,253) matches the variant rows joined to products.\n- Rows are sorted by `product_revenue` descending.\n\n**Choices I made**\n- **Order filter:** I used `orders.status` and excluded `CANCELLED`, `RETURNED`, and `FAILED`, as the spec says. `FAILED` doesn't occur in the data.\n- **Revenue:** `product_revenue` is `QUANTITY_ORDERED * UNIT_PRICE`, the same definition the existing `fct_product_sales_performance` model uses. I did not use `LINE_TOTAL`, which may include discounts and tax.\n- **`avg_unit_price`:** this is `product_revenue / units_sold`, the weighted average the spec asks for. It is NULL when a product has no units sold, rather than 0 or a divide-by-zero error.\n- **`total_orders`:** this is the count of distinct valid orders per product. It is lower than the raw line count (2,913 against 2,961) because an order with two lines for the same product counts once.\n- **Fan-out:** order lines are aggregated to product grain in their own CTE, and variants are aggregated separately. Neither is joined to the other, so the variant count is not multiplied by order lines.\n- **Orphans:** the product list is the anchor, so 15 order lines whose product is missing from the products table are excluded. 18 order lines whose order is missing are also excluded, because their status cannot be determined.\n- **Variants:** `total_variants` counts all variants, including inactive ones.\n\n**Things to be aware of**\n- The model was created as `main.fct_product_metrics`, not in a `marts` schema. The `dbt_project.yml` config for `marts` is keyed under `retail_warehouse`, which does not match the project name `retail_dw_master`, so it doesn't apply. I did not change that config.\n- I did not modify `profiles.yml`. It already uses the profile `retail_dw_master` with a relative DuckDB path, and that path worked. It does not read `$DUCKDB_PATH`.\n\nVERDICT: fixed", "verdict": null}
{"event": "attempt_end", "t": 1795260242.559, "attempt": 1, "passed": true, "failed_check": null, "checks": [{"name": "tamper", "passed": true, "detail": "1 changed file(s), all allowed; all 929 test(s) unchanged"}, {"name": "masking", "passed": true, "detail": "no model disabled, no rows filtered away"}, {"name": "clean_rebuild", "passed": true, "detail": "dbt build passed: 2871 node(s); 293 node(s) that already failed before the change, none downstream of it, still fail: model.retail_dw_master.COMP_OPERATIONS_YOY; model.retail_dw_master.comp_customers__mom; model.retail_dw_master.comp_customers__qoq; model.retail_dw_master.comp_customers__wow; model.retail_dw_master.comp_customers__yoy; model.retail_dw_master.comp_finance__mom; model.retail_dw_master.comp_finance__qoq; model.retail_dw_master.comp_finance__wow; and 285 more"}, {"name": "collateral", "passed": true, "detail": "2211 model(s) outside the lineage unchanged (222 compared by row count only and 0 not compared, because they differ between builds of the unchanged project)"}], "duration_s": 130.0, "diff": "diff --git a/models/marts/product/fct_product_metrics.sql b/models/marts/product/fct_product_metrics.sql\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/models/marts/product/fct_product_metrics.sql\n@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@\n+{{\n+    config(\n+        materialized='table'\n+    )\n+}}\n+\n+-- Product-level performance summary.\n+-- Grain: one row per product (all products, including those with no sales).\n+--\n+-- Fan-out protection: order lines are aggregated to product grain in their own\n+-- CTE, and variants are aggregated to product grain separately. Neither is\n+-- joined to the other, so variant counts are not multiplied by order lines\n+-- and vice versa.\n+\n+with products as (\n+    select\n+        product_id,\n+        product_name,\n+        primary_category_id\n+    from {{ ref('stg_product__products') }}\n+),\n+\n+categories as (\n+    select\n+        category_id,\n+        category_name\n+    from {{ ref('stg_product__product_categories') }}\n+),\n+\n+-- Valid completed sales only. Order-level status drives the filter.\n+valid_orders as (\n+    select\n+        order_id\n+    from {{ ref('stg_orders__orders') }}\n+    where status not in ('CANCELLED', 'RETURNED', 'FAILED')\n+),\n+\n+sales_by_product as (\n+    select\n+        ol.product_id,\n+        count(distinct ol.order_id)                          as total_orders,\n+        sum(ol.QUANTITY_ORDERED)                             as units_sold,\n+        sum(ol.QUANTITY_ORDERED * ol.UNIT_PRICE)             as product_revenue\n+    from {{ ref('stg_orders__order_lines') }} ol\n+    inner join valid_orders vo\n+        on ol.order_id = vo.order_id\n+    group by 1\n+),\n+\n+variants_by_product as (\n+    select\n+        product_id,\n+        count(distinct variant_id) as total_variants\n+    from {{ ref('stg_product__product_variants') }}\n+    group by 1\n+)\n+\n+select\n+    p.product_id,\n+    p.product_name,\n+    c.category_name                                          as category,\n+    coalesce(s.total_orders, 0)                              as total_orders,\n+    coalesce(s.units_sold, 0)                                as units_sold,\n+    coalesce(s.product_revenue, 0)                           as product_revenue,\n+    -- Weighted average: total revenue / total units, not AVG(unit_price)\n+    s.product_revenue / nullif(s.units_sold, 0)              as avg_unit_price,\n+    coalesce(v.total_variants, 0)                            as total_variants\n+from products p\n+left join categories c\n+    on p.primary_category_id = c.category_id\n+left join sales_by_product s\n+    on p.product_id = s.product_id\n+left join variants_by_product v\n+    on p.product_id = v.product_id\n+order by product_revenue desc\n"}
